<p><a name="fn8"></a>8. For example, both August and September 2021 employment reports suggested job growth at much lower levels than consensus forecasts and were subsequently sizably increased. Similarly, based on current data, PCE inflation for 2021:Q3 to 2022:Q2 are also revised higher. See the real-time data for macroeconomists on the Federal Reserve Bank of Philadelphia's website at <a href="https://www.philadelphiafed.org/surveys-and-data/real-time-data-research/pcon">https://www.philadelphiafed.org/surveys-and-data/real-time-data-research/pcon</a>. <a href="#f8">Return to text</a></p>

